NAME
       sudo - run a command as root

SYNOPSIS
       **sudo** __command__ [__arg__...]
       **sudo -i**
       **sudo -s**

DESCRIPTION
       Ask for the password of the current user and run __command__ with
       root privileges. Only members of the **wheel** group in /etc/group
       may use sudo; the installer adds users to it when they are given
       administrator rights.

       The password is checked by the kernel against /etc/shadow. After
       three wrong passwords sudo gives up. Every attempt is written to the
       kernel log, see journalctl(1).

OPTIONS
       **-i**
           Start a root login shell in /root.

       **-s**
           Start a root shell in the current directory.

ENVIRONMENT
       **SUDO_USER** is set to the name of the user who ran sudo. **USER** and
       **LOGNAME** are set to root.

EXIT STATUS
       The exit status of __command__, 1 when authentication fails, 126 when
       the command cannot run and 127 when it is not found.

EXAMPLES
       sudo rm /etc/motd
       sudo -i

SEE ALSO
       id(1), sh(1)
